{
  "case_id": "2020-19-292",
  "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "KELSI B. CORKRAN (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the early morning, Respondents approached Roxanne Torres in her car and attempted to open the door without announcing they were police officers. Believing she was being car-jacked, Ms. Torres drove away, and as she did, Respondents fired 13 shots at her. Two of the bullets hit her in the back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Ms. Corkran, what if the police had shot out the tires of her car, but she was able to continue driving on? You know, they were those self-sealing tires that you can get. Would that be a seizure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this was an individual who had thrown drugs away and then was later tackled, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying Justice Scalia was -- it's not only precedent, but Justice Scalia was right, or are you not saying that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are a lot of cases about private citizens, you know, mere touches and -- and all that, that, nonetheless, are held to constitute an arrest. Is that the same? Is there any reason we shouldn't translate those into police effecting a seizure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Standridge",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STANDRIDGE: Absolutely, Mr. Chief Justice. We should not translate that body of case law cited by the Petitioner regarding the mere touch rule because it arose in a very limited and narrow context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Standridge",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STANDRIDGE: Absolutely, Justice Thomas. The -- the simple fact of the matter is that Hodari D. did not involve a use of force, as did Brower versus County of Inyo and the present case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, your colleagues on the other side suggest that your rule will lead to tricky line-drawing problems. What -- what --what do you say to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: The other side makes a point, and I think Justice Breyer was getting at this, there's some symmetry with Jones, the GPS case, of placing a GPS on your car, intent to search, touching your body with intent to restrain."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c7d2c11e5b26972448426c3bd21a2c2f494873925696c87001ecd1070f22852",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c7d2c11e5b2-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
